format: 2
name: a diamond Tuple2 of BigIntegers encodes its components (#299)
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 03
arg: 04
expect: AGREE
note: ADR-068 D4 exception 2 (#299): `new Tuple2<>(x, y)` resolved to a tuple with Data components, so the
note: BigIntegers were put in the constructor unencoded and the script failed (MkCons) where the JVM returns 4, at
note: every level. The component types are now inferred as javac infers them (from the declared target type, else
note: from the arguments) and each component is encoded by its type, as `new Tuple2<BigInteger, BigInteger>(x, y)`
note: does. recorded.base is the reference frontend at B0.
recorded.jvm: Value 04 []
recorded.base: Failure [] "MkCons: element type Integer[] does not match list element type Data[]"
---
import java.math.BigInteger;
import org.julclang.core.types.Tuple2;

public class Probe {

    public static BigInteger m(BigInteger x, BigInteger y) {
        var t = new Tuple2<>(x, y);
        BigInteger s = t.second();
        return s;
    }
}
